{"name":"In the Spotlight","hex":"#ede6ed","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"in the spotlight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Prepositional phrase","definitions":["In the focus of attention, especially from the media."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/in_the_spotlight"}],"entries":[{"title":"In the Spotlight","blocks":[{"text":"In the Spotlight is the fifteenth studio album by the American singer-songwriter and bass guitar player Suzi Quatro."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7d/Suzi_Quatro_In_the_Spotlight_album_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_the_Spotlight","wikidata":"Q11170536"},{"title":"Spotlight (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Spotlight is a 2015 American biographical drama film directed by Tom McCarthy and written by McCarthy and Josh Singer. The film follows The Boston Globe's \"Spotlight\" team, the oldest continuously operating newspaper investigative journalist unit in the United States, and its investigation into a decades-long coverup of widespread and systemic child sex abuse by numerous priests of the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Boston. Although the plot was original, it is based on a series of stories by the Spotlight team that earned The Globe the 2003 Pulitzer Prize for Public Service. The film features an ensemble cast including Mark Ruffalo, Michael Keaton, Rachel McAdams, John Slattery, Stanley Tucci, Brian d'Arcy James, Liev Schreiber, and Billy Crudup."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f3/Spotlight_%28film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spotlight_(film)","wikidata":"Q18154496"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Mark_Ruffalo_June_2014.jpg/500px-Mark_Ruffalo_June_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna